  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Four players receive 13 cards each. An auction determines the contract (trump or no-trump) and forms a temporary partnership: the highest bidder is the Declarer and the player who accepts the bid becomes the Acceptor; the other two defend. The Acceptor's hand is exposed as dummy after the opening lead. Players then play 13 tricks: must follow suit if possible; highest card of the led suit wins the trick, or a trump wins if unable to follow. Points are scored individually (above and below the line); the side that wins two games wins the rubber.",
    Player: "Four players receive 13 cards each. An auction determines the contract (trump or no-trump) and forms a temporary partnership: the highest bidder is the Declarer and the player who accepts the bid becomes the Acceptor; the other two defend. The Acceptor's hand is exposed as dummy after the opening lead. Players then play 13 tricks: must follow suit if possible; highest card of the led suit wins the trick, or a trump wins if unable to follow. Points are scored individually (above and below the line); the side that wins two games wins the rubber.",
    objective: 'Score the most points individually over a Rubber. Gains are tracked per player, not per team.',
    gameplay: "Four players receive 13 cards each. An auction determines the contract (trump or no-trump) and forms a temporary partnership: the highest bidder is the Declarer and the player who accepts the bid becomes the Acceptor; the other two defend. The Acceptor's hand is exposed as dummy after the opening lead. Players then play 13 tricks: must follow suit if possible; highest card of the led suit wins the trick, or a trump wins if unable to follow. Points are scored individually (above and below the line); the side that wins two games wins the rubber.",
    keyRules: [
      'Deal 13 cards each; no fixed partners.',
      'Auction establishes contract and temporary Declarer-Acceptor partnership.',
      'Must follow suit when possible; highest of led suit or trump wins the trick.',
      'Individual scoring over a rubber; first to two games wins the rubber.',
